exports[`buildPrompt > builds a prompt from only a hue 1`] = `
"Follow the Palletter skill below to create color palettes for this request.

<skill path="SKILL.md">
Skill body.
</skill>

# Palette request

## Hues

- #2563eb (oklch(54.6% 0.215 262.9)). An exact color (see SKILL.md, step 4).

## Schemes

Make one palette for each of these schemes, in this order. The base hue is 262.9°, from the first hue.

- monochromatic: hue 262.9°.

## Steps

Every color must have exactly these steps: 50, 100, 200, 300, 400, 500, 600, 700, 800, 900, 950.

## Names

Name each color after what it is, such as "brand", "accent", "sand", or "ocean".

## Decide yourself

The user left these to you: the mood, the saturation, how many colors each palette has (see SKILL.md, step 2). Choose what makes the best palette, and mention your choices in the rationale.

Reply with a single \`\`\`json code block in the response format from SKILL.md, and nothing else.
"
`;

exports[`buildPrompt > builds a prompt with every option set 1`] = `
"Follow the Palletter skill below to create color palettes for this request.

<skill path="SKILL.md">
Skill body.
</skill>

# Palette request

## Hues

- "terracotta": #e2725b (oklch(67.7% 0.144 32.9)). An exact color (see SKILL.md, step 4).
- "sage". The user named this color; choose a value that matches the name.

## Mood

"warm and welcoming"

## Schemes

Make one palette for each of these schemes, in this order. The base hue is 32.9°, from the first hue.

- complementary: reference hues 32.9°, 212.9° (offsets 0°, +180° from 32.9°).
- triadic: reference hues 32.9°, 152.9°, 272.9° (offsets 0°, +120°, +240° from 32.9°).

## Steps

Every color must have exactly these steps: 100, 200, 300.

## Saturation

muted (see saturation-and-mood.md)

## Roles

Make one color for each role, and set its \`role\` to the name below.

- "primary": warm (see saturation-and-mood.md)
- "secondary"

## Names

Name each color after its hue in plain words, such as "blue", "coral", or "sage". Tokens will be named like \`--brand-[color]-[step]\`.

Reply with a single \`\`\`json code block in the response format from SKILL.md, and nothing else.
"
`;
